# 4. APPROVED ARCHITECTURAL DECISIONS

The following decisions have been explicitly approved and must not be changed.

## 4.1 Category ownership

Category belongs exclusively to Branch Item Availability.

- Remove Category from Global Item Master.
- Remove Category from Global Item Creation Audit.
- Remove Category as a mandatory global code-generation dimension.
- Remove Category as a mandatory global description-generation dimension.
- Assign Category separately for each Company and Branch.
- The same Global Item may have different Categories in different branches.
- Maintain one active Category assignment per Global Item, Company and Branch, unless an approved future requirement changes this rule.

## 4.2 UOM ownership

Global UOM defaults with authorized branch-specific overrides.

Global Item Master maintains:

- Default Purchase UOM.
- Default Inventory / Base UOM.
- Default conversion definition.
- Conversion precision.
- Rounding rules.
- Valid UOM relationships.

Branch Item Availability may maintain:

- Branch Purchase UOM.
- Branch Inventory UOM.
- Branch conversion definition.
- Conversion numerator.
- Conversion denominator.
- Conversion precision.
- Rounding rule.

A valid conversion is mandatory whenever the effective Purchase UOM differs from the effective Inventory UOM.

Branch overrides must be authorized and audited.

## 4.3 Global Item Code

One globally unique Global Item Code.

- Generate once.
- Reuse across all branches.
- Do not generate a different global code for each branch.
- Do not require Category for global code generation.
- Do not create duplicate Global Item records.

## 4.4 Compliance ownership

All operational controls and compliance settings belong at Branch Item Availability level.

Do not maintain global operational compliance defaults.

## 4.5 Approval workflow

Two independent approval stages are mandatory:

**Stage 1:** Global Item Creation → Global Checker Approval.

**Stage 2:** Branch Item Activation → Branch Checker Approval.

Global approval does not automatically activate an item in any branch.

Branch approval does not modify the Global Item identity.

Only an approved and active Branch Item Availability record may be selected in a new PR.

