# 14. DUAL APPROVAL WORKFLOW

Implement two independent approval workflows.

## 14.1 Global Item Approval

1. Authorized user creates Global Item.
2. User saves draft.
3. System generates provisional Global Item Code.
4. System generates provisional Global Item Description.
5. User executes Global Item Creation Audit.
6. Mandatory errors are resolved.
7. User submits for Checker Approval.
8. Checker reviews the Global Item and audit results.
9. Checker approves or rejects.
10. Approved Global Item becomes eligible for Branch Item Availability.

A draft or rejected Global Item must not be selectable for branch activation.

## 14.2 Branch Item Approval

1. Authorized user selects approved Global Item.
2. Selects Company and Branch.
3. Configures Category.
4. Configures branch UOM overrides where required.
5. Configures purchasing and inventory settings.
6. Configures compliance.
7. Configures attachments and other optional controls.
8. Executes Branch Item Activation Audit.
9. Resolves mandatory errors.
10. Submits for Branch Checker Approval.
11. Checker reviews branch configuration and audit.
12. Checker approves or rejects.
13. Approved record becomes active for that branch.

Approval must use existing KOSH RBAC and approval services.

The creator must not approve their own record unless an existing formally approved policy explicitly permits it.

